Subject: Default PHP 7.4 to a size-tracking system allocator under Fil-C
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted

The PHP 7.4 counterpart of php-8.4-alloc-filc.patch. Zend's allocator hands
out request memory from 2 MiB chunks, so Fil-C bounds a PHP value only by
its chunk and reuses freed values' memory inside it. Use after free and
overflows between values then go unnoticed. Make the tracked system
allocator the default; USE_ZEND_ALLOC=1 restores Zend's allocator and
USE_TRACKED_ALLOC=0 selects untracked malloc.

PHP 7.4's tracked allocator records only addresses, for freeing leftovers at
the end of a request, so it had no memory_limit and memory_get_usage()
reported 0. Under Fil-C, keep each allocation's size as PHP 8 does,
enforce the limit, count usage and peaks, and answer zend_mem_block_size()
and is_zend_ptr() from the table.

tracked_free_all() frees by addresses kept as integers, which have no
capability under Fil-C; leave leftover request memory to the collector.

